.TH New-HomebridgeLocation 1 "December 2025" "docker-homebridge" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
New-HomebridgeLocation \- Generate Homebridge artifacts and certificates for a location
.SH SYNOPSIS
New-HomebridgeLocation [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Generates location-specific artifacts for Homebridge deployment, including:
.IP \(bu 2
Certificate request configuration (secrets/certificates/LOCATION/certificate-request.conf)
.IP \(bu 2
Docker Compose file (homebridge-LOCATION.yaml)
.IP \(bu 2
Environment variables file (homebridge-LOCATION.env)
.PP
The script supports two modes of operation:
.IP 1. 3
Load all parameters from an environment file using --env-file
.IP 2. 3
Specify individual parameters via command-line options
.PP
All parameters are required and must be provided through one of these methods.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --env-file <file>
Load all environment variables from the specified file. The file should contain KEY=VALUE pairs for: LOCATION, COUNTRY_CODE, STATE_OR_PROVINCE, CITY, ORGANIZATION_NAME, ORGANIZATIONAL_UNIT, DOMAIN_NAME, EMAIL_ADDRESS.
.TP
.B -l, --location <location>
Set the location name (e.g., us-wa). Used in file names and certificate generation.
.TP
.B -c, --country-code <code>
Two-letter country code (e.g., US).
.TP
.B -s, --state-or-province <state>
State or province name.
.TP
.B -C, --city <city>
City name.
.TP
.B -O, --organization-name <org>
Organization name for certificates.
.TP
.B -U, --organizational-unit <unit>
Organizational unit for certificates.
.TP
.B -D, --domain-name <domain>
Fully qualified domain name.
.TP
.B -E, --email-address <email>
Email address for certificate requests.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show usage information and exit.
.SH GENERATED FILES
.TP
.I secrets/certificates/LOCATION/certificate-request.conf
OpenSSL certificate request configuration file generated from the template.
.TP
.I homebridge-LOCATION.yaml
Docker Compose file for the Homebridge service at this location.
.TP
.I homebridge-LOCATION.env
Environment variables file containing all the specified parameters for future reference.
.SH USAGE
.SS Using an environment file:
.RS
.nf
\fB./build/New-HomebridgeLocation --env-file=homebridge-us-wa.env\fR
.fi
.RE
.SS Using command-line options:
.RS
.nf
\fB./build/New-HomebridgeLocation \\
  --location=us-wa \\
  --country-code=US \\
  --state-or-province=Washington \\
  --city=Seattle \\
  --organization-name="My Organization" \\
  --organizational-unit="IT Department" \\
  --domain-name=example.com \\
  --email-address=admin@example.com\fR
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success
.TP
1
Error (missing required parameters, template not found, etc.)
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.TP
.B Required:
envsubst (from gettext package)
.TP
.B Templates:
build/templates/certificate-request.conf.template
.br
homebridge.yaml.template
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR envsubst (1),
.BR openssl (1)
